1
00:00:00,730 --> 00:00:06,755
(A Bona fide Killer)

2
00:00:08,765 --> 00:00:10,588
(This drama, its characters,
and events are fictional.)

3
00:00:10,612 --> 00:00:11,761
(Scenes with child actors
and animals were supervised.)

4
00:00:12,515 --> 00:00:14,881
(Episode 9)

5
00:00:29,216 --> 00:00:30,984
You scared me.

6
00:00:33,120 --> 00:00:35,355
- What is it?
- What?

7
00:00:36,890 --> 00:00:40,894
I feel like I said something important
and heard something even more important.

8
00:00:43,697 --> 00:00:46,266
I never knew there was honey tea
in the break room.

9
00:00:48,569 --> 00:00:51,405
Look, you barely ever drink,
and then you went and knocked them back.

10
00:00:51,438 --> 00:00:53,907
You should have just gone home
and collapsed into bed.

11
00:00:53,907 --> 00:00:55,175
Why did you come in on a weekend?

12
00:00:55,576 --> 00:00:57,211
Why did you come in?

13
00:00:58,679 --> 00:00:59,746
Me?

14
00:00:59,746 --> 00:01:02,516
Are you seriously asking me that?
You really want to know?

15
00:01:03,117 --> 00:01:05,552
Goodness. In that case,

16
00:01:06,353 --> 00:01:08,188
should I give you a heartfelt answer?

17
00:01:09,723 --> 00:01:11,825
Look into the body found
at the Hyeonsa-dong villa, okay?

18
00:01:11,825 --> 00:01:14,895
Pull a list of recently released convicts
who got off too easy.

19
00:01:14,895 --> 00:01:16,230
You're giving me a headache.

20
00:01:16,697 --> 00:01:19,133
My head is already
not functioning right now.

21
00:01:20,334 --> 00:01:21,468
And that's not all. This.

22
00:01:22,269 --> 00:01:23,504
Do you see this? Do you?

23
00:01:23,504 --> 00:01:25,405
The never-ending pile of Kingfisher files.

24
00:01:25,973 --> 00:01:28,575
- This is why I...
- Should I give you a test again?

25
00:01:33,247 --> 00:01:35,149
Let's see. Today...

26
00:01:36,316 --> 00:01:37,384
"The Haegong-dong gosiwon."

27
00:01:37,417 --> 00:01:38,852
This is that one.

28
00:01:38,852 --> 00:01:40,788
Kingfisher's last case
before disappearing.

29
00:01:41,455 --> 00:01:44,057
Finally, the end is in sight.

30
00:01:48,195 --> 00:01:49,430
(Case Summary: 4 p.m.,
At a gosiwon in Haegong-Dong...)

31
00:01:50,964 --> 00:01:52,099
What?

32
00:01:53,300 --> 00:01:55,402
There was a seven-year-old kid
at the crime scene?

33
00:01:56,103 --> 00:01:57,271
But...

34
00:01:57,304 --> 00:01:59,206
there's a side of him
people don't know about.

35
00:01:59,940 --> 00:02:02,743
Right in front of
the victim's seven-year-old son,

36
00:02:03,143 --> 00:02:05,546
the bastard shot and killed him.

37
00:02:06,780 --> 00:02:10,984
I actually know.
I'm telling you, I saw Kingfisher.

38
00:02:12,886 --> 00:02:14,188
That day in Haegong-dong...

39
00:02:15,155 --> 00:02:18,325
The Gosiwon Case. I was there.

40
00:02:18,358 --> 00:02:19,993
Whoa, you scared me.

41
00:02:23,063 --> 00:02:24,364
Bo Na.

42
00:02:24,364 --> 00:02:26,600
I called, but you didn't answer,
so I left a message.

43
00:02:26,600 --> 00:02:27,601
Did you just see it?

44
00:02:28,469 --> 00:02:29,770
Playing tricks again, I see.

45
00:02:29,803 --> 00:02:31,138
Oh, come on.

46
00:02:31,805 --> 00:02:33,974
I figured you'd be home
since it's the weekend.

47
00:02:34,541 --> 00:02:36,577
Was I being too rude?

48
00:02:37,744 --> 00:02:38,779
Should I wait outside?

49
00:02:39,980 --> 00:02:42,249
If you don't mind, you can wait inside.

50
00:02:47,020 --> 00:02:48,956
Bo Na, is that okay?

51
00:02:51,658 --> 00:02:53,360
Listen carefully.

52
00:02:53,994 --> 00:02:55,329
If you say one unnecessary word,

53
00:02:55,896 --> 00:02:57,664
you're dead by my hand.

54
00:02:59,032 --> 00:03:01,535
That hurts. You don't trust me?

55
00:03:01,935 --> 00:03:02,936
Before,

56
00:03:03,403 --> 00:03:06,206
and now, even more so since "that day,"

57
00:03:06,807 --> 00:03:10,744
if you don't want to die,
remember what I said.

58
00:03:10,744 --> 00:03:12,513
Thanks for the warm welcome, Bo Na.

59
00:03:14,148 --> 00:03:16,150
Hurry up. I miss you.

60
00:03:19,953 --> 00:03:21,021
Please, come in.

61
00:03:29,797 --> 00:03:32,232
Congratulations. You're pregnant.

62
00:03:32,866 --> 00:03:34,034
You're five weeks along.

63
00:03:35,803 --> 00:03:38,205
See this tiny little dot right here?

64
00:03:38,739 --> 00:03:39,873
That's the gestational sac.

65
00:03:39,907 --> 00:03:41,542
The gestational sac?

66
00:03:41,575 --> 00:03:42,676
Yes.

67
00:03:44,044 --> 00:03:45,446
(Maternity Handbook Daon Song Ob-Gyn)

68
00:03:45,446 --> 00:03:46,747
<i>You know you need to be very careful...</i>

69
00:03:46,780 --> 00:03:48,415
<i>since you're still in the early stages,</i>
<i>right?</i>

70
00:03:48,449 --> 00:03:52,252
<i>Avoid running, intense exercise,</i>
<i>and lifting heavy objects.</i>

71
00:03:52,252 --> 00:03:54,021
<i>Going up and down stairs quickly,</i>

72
00:03:54,021 --> 00:03:58,325
or suddenly sitting down
and standing up should also be avoided.

73
00:03:58,725 --> 00:04:01,628
Above all, try to stay relaxed.

74
00:04:02,463 --> 00:04:04,932
Stress can have
a negative effect on the baby.

75
00:04:09,803 --> 00:04:13,140
(My Santa)

76
00:04:15,442 --> 00:04:18,045
(My Santa)

77
00:04:19,646 --> 00:04:20,747
(My Santa)

78
00:04:22,683 --> 00:04:23,750
Tae Sung.

79
00:04:23,750 --> 00:04:25,853
Yes, honey. Did you eat lunch?

80
00:04:25,853 --> 00:04:28,255
Of course I did.
It's already late. Did you?

81
00:04:28,689 --> 00:04:32,159
I'm on my way to eat now.
I just finished up my reporting.

82
00:04:33,060 --> 00:04:34,128
You must be hungry.

83
00:04:34,695 --> 00:04:35,763
Why do you sound like that?

84
00:04:36,497 --> 00:04:38,298
Are you sick?

85
00:04:40,534 --> 00:04:42,803
No, I'm fine. Why?

86
00:04:45,672 --> 00:04:46,707
Will you be late tonight?

87
00:04:47,474 --> 00:04:49,743
Even if I leave right after I eat,

88
00:04:51,111 --> 00:04:52,646
I have to stop by the office
to wrap things up,

89
00:04:52,646 --> 00:04:53,847
so it'll be evening
by the time I get home.

90
00:04:55,082 --> 00:04:56,150
I wish you could come home early.

91
00:04:56,884 --> 00:04:58,118
So we can have dinner together.

92
00:04:58,619 --> 00:05:00,087
And I have something to show you.

93
00:05:00,988 --> 00:05:02,623
Of course.
I'll get there as early as I can.

94
00:05:02,623 --> 00:05:04,258
I'll wrap this up and fly over.

95
00:05:15,869 --> 00:05:18,005
Have you decided
what you're going to do now?

96
00:05:18,572 --> 00:05:20,808
Well, I was thinking
of using my severance pay...

97
00:05:20,841 --> 00:05:22,743
to open a small shop, but...

98
00:05:23,210 --> 00:05:24,478
nothing comes to mind.

99
00:05:25,078 --> 00:05:27,080
If I had it my way,

100
00:05:27,080 --> 00:05:30,517
I'd spend the rest of my life
surrounded by beautiful things.

101
00:05:31,318 --> 00:05:33,554
You could open a flower shop.
Flowers are beautiful, right?

102
00:05:36,156 --> 00:05:38,225
Well, well.

103
00:05:38,859 --> 00:05:42,596
Yu Bo Na even knows flowers are pretty.
My, how times have changed.

104
00:05:43,530 --> 00:05:46,300
Then again, the world has changed.

105
00:05:46,900 --> 00:05:47,901
Yu Bo Na's world, that is.

106
00:05:49,103 --> 00:05:51,238
Your face has really brightened up.

107
00:05:51,972 --> 00:05:53,373
Married life must be treating you well.

108
00:06:03,884 --> 00:06:05,185
When you have a baby,

109
00:06:06,353 --> 00:06:08,155
does the world really change?

110
00:06:14,027 --> 00:06:15,329
Are you planning to get pregnant?

111
00:06:18,832 --> 00:06:20,267
But it's just a vague idea.

112
00:06:20,901 --> 00:06:21,969
And it's scary.

113
00:06:22,703 --> 00:06:24,872
It's just that the word "mom" feels so...

114
00:06:26,006 --> 00:06:27,708
distant from who I am...

115
00:06:27,741 --> 00:06:29,343
You worry about the strangest things.

116
00:06:29,743 --> 00:06:31,445
You're still the same person
after becoming a mom.

117
00:06:31,478 --> 00:06:32,946
Your world doesn't change.

118
00:06:32,980 --> 00:06:34,348
It just gets bigger.

119
00:06:34,848 --> 00:06:38,585
That's what my grandma used to say.

120
00:06:38,585 --> 00:06:39,987
And I thought so too.

121
00:06:43,223 --> 00:06:44,792
Do you really think I can do a good job?

122
00:06:45,325 --> 00:06:46,593
You're already doing a great job.

123
00:06:48,462 --> 00:06:51,198
Instead of that coffee you love,

124
00:06:51,231 --> 00:06:52,533
you have a cup of herbal tea.

125
00:06:57,070 --> 00:06:58,138
Don't worry.

126
00:06:58,639 --> 00:07:00,941
Your world has already changed
once before, Bo Na.

127
00:07:01,341 --> 00:07:05,245
From now on,
it will only expand and become stronger.

128
00:07:21,862 --> 00:07:23,297
- Yes, Team Leader.
- Manager Yu.

129
00:07:23,330 --> 00:07:26,633
Today's meeting
with Yeon Cheon Bok is off.

130
00:07:26,633 --> 00:07:28,402
That son of a bitch.

131
00:07:28,402 --> 00:07:31,738
He made his move before Manager Go could.

132
00:07:33,273 --> 00:07:36,143
I'm chasing him now.
He's escaping in a taxi.

133
00:07:36,477 --> 00:07:39,313
- He moved faster than we thought.
- I know.

134
00:07:39,313 --> 00:07:42,683
Who would've thought he'd bolt
right after getting to the hospital?

135
00:07:43,150 --> 00:07:45,419
If we lose him now,

136
00:07:45,419 --> 00:07:48,489
it'll be even harder to catch him later.

137
00:07:49,356 --> 00:07:51,592
We'll have to change the plan. I'll go.

138
00:07:52,526 --> 00:07:53,894
Keep me updated on his route.

139
00:07:58,031 --> 00:07:59,500
(Maternity Handbook)

140
00:09:05,966 --> 00:09:07,201
Here you go.

141
00:09:19,079 --> 00:09:20,447
- Team Leader.
- Yes?

142
00:09:20,447 --> 00:09:22,416
Yeon Cheon Bok's mother and son are here.

143
00:09:22,449 --> 00:09:26,553
His son? You mean the infant his mother
had with her at the time of the arrest?

144
00:09:26,587 --> 00:09:29,623
Yes, I'll wait until they leave.

145
00:09:29,623 --> 00:09:31,458
The police will be raiding the place
any minute...

146
00:09:31,492 --> 00:09:34,161
- This is grim.
- We can't do it in front of the child.

147
00:09:34,761 --> 00:09:35,896
I'll wait.

148
00:09:39,032 --> 00:09:40,400
Surprise.

149
00:09:40,434 --> 00:09:41,702
Hey there, partner.

150
00:09:54,515 --> 00:09:57,050
- There he is again. See?
- Just like Daddy said, there he is.

151
00:09:57,084 --> 00:09:59,620
- See?
- Daddy, the doll is right here.

152
00:09:59,620 --> 00:10:01,588
See? Isn't it cool?

153
00:10:02,156 --> 00:10:03,524
- And another one.
- Another one.

154
00:10:04,424 --> 00:10:05,425
Honey, you're home?

155
00:10:06,426 --> 00:10:09,897
Mommy, Mommy.
A doll keeps coming out of the doll.

156
00:10:09,930 --> 00:10:13,867
- Oh, really?
- Sergei bought Yul another present.

157
00:10:15,636 --> 00:10:18,305
- You could have given me a heads-up.
- Surprise.

158
00:10:20,307 --> 00:10:21,408
Hello, brother.

159
00:10:23,544 --> 00:10:25,245
It's here, it's here.

160
00:10:25,245 --> 00:10:26,914
- What?
- The chicken. The chicken's here.

161
00:10:27,848 --> 00:10:30,818
I think your husband is jealous of us.

162
00:10:31,885 --> 00:10:33,987
Behave yourself.

163
00:10:35,989 --> 00:10:39,193
I didn't have anything to
serve, so I asked my sister for a favor.

164
00:10:40,494 --> 00:10:42,396
But I could have taken them out to eat.

165
00:10:43,130 --> 00:10:45,766
You're not even feeling well.
Why go to all this trouble?

166
00:10:45,766 --> 00:10:47,000
No, it's fine. Besides,

167
00:10:47,501 --> 00:10:49,536
I told you I wanted
to meet your Russian friend...

168
00:10:52,272 --> 00:10:54,641
though I didn't know
he was a guy like that.

169
00:10:54,675 --> 00:10:57,711
Did I not tell you he was a guy?
I'm pretty sure I did.

170
00:10:58,378 --> 00:10:59,813
You said he was a man.

171
00:11:01,548 --> 00:11:03,884
You didn't say he was so handsome.

172
00:11:04,618 --> 00:11:07,688
- What? You think he's handsome?
- What?

173
00:11:08,522 --> 00:11:09,656
He's good-looking.

174
00:11:13,060 --> 00:11:14,361
- All right.
- All right.

175
00:11:14,361 --> 00:11:16,563
(Taesung Chicken)

176
00:11:19,933 --> 00:11:22,236
- Korean chicken really is the best.
- Do you want this?

177
00:11:22,803 --> 00:11:24,071
This is really delicious.

178
00:11:24,104 --> 00:11:26,473
I'm glad you like it.

179
00:11:26,507 --> 00:11:28,041
So, Sergei...

180
00:11:29,176 --> 00:11:33,580
Please, just call me Seul Gi.
I'd prefer that.

181
00:11:33,614 --> 00:11:34,715
Okay.

182
00:11:37,351 --> 00:11:40,854
Seul Gi, I heard you were born in Russia.

183
00:11:41,722 --> 00:11:43,090
Your Korean is excellent.

184
00:11:43,123 --> 00:11:45,559
That's because my mama is Korean.

185
00:11:46,960 --> 00:11:50,230
And since I grew up playing with Bo Na,
I guess I just got used to it.

186
00:11:54,501 --> 00:11:56,036
We lived in the same neighborhood.

187
00:11:56,770 --> 00:11:59,206
- I see.
- Was I eight...

188
00:11:59,239 --> 00:12:00,707
when I first met Bo Na?

189
00:12:01,175 --> 00:12:03,210
It was right after you moved to Russia,
right?

190
00:12:04,044 --> 00:12:05,078
That's right.

191
00:12:05,846 --> 00:12:07,714
So you two go way back.

192
00:12:09,450 --> 00:12:10,551
We do, right?

193
00:12:11,819 --> 00:12:13,720
But are you okay, honey?

194
00:12:14,154 --> 00:12:17,624
I mean, he came home
blackout drunk last night.

195
00:12:17,658 --> 00:12:19,960
You must be exhausted.
Can you even stomach this right now?

196
00:12:19,960 --> 00:12:21,028
No, I'm fine. Really, I'm fine.

197
00:12:21,028 --> 00:12:23,397
I'm just happy to be hearing stories
about your past.

198
00:12:24,531 --> 00:12:26,633
It's delicious. I'm fine.

199
00:12:27,267 --> 00:12:28,535
The first day I met Bo Na,

200
00:12:29,036 --> 00:12:33,707
I said, "Hello? I'm Sergei."
I said that in Korean, and she went,

201
00:12:34,408 --> 00:12:35,609
"Seul Gi?"

202
00:12:36,310 --> 00:12:37,411
"No, Sergei."

203
00:12:38,812 --> 00:12:41,281
I see. "No Seul Gi?"

204
00:12:47,521 --> 00:12:51,258
- From that day on, to Bo Na, I became...
- Right.

205
00:12:51,291 --> 00:12:52,759
I became No Seul Gi.

206
00:12:52,759 --> 00:12:54,528
So that's the story behind your name.

207
00:12:54,862 --> 00:12:58,298
Yul, chew this slowly and carefully, okay?

208
00:12:58,332 --> 00:12:59,633
You eat some too, Mommy.

209
00:13:00,234 --> 00:13:01,235
Is this for me?

210
00:13:02,903 --> 00:13:04,671
It's delicious. Thank you.

211
00:13:04,671 --> 00:13:05,739
Bo Na, you eat chicken?

212
00:13:06,507 --> 00:13:07,574
You never used to like chicken.

213
00:13:08,342 --> 00:13:10,310
- I eat it now.
- You do?

214
00:13:11,345 --> 00:13:13,347
That's strange. Before, chicken...

215
00:13:14,715 --> 00:13:15,816
Chicken porridge.

216
00:13:16,850 --> 00:13:17,951
You hate chicken porridge too.

217
00:13:21,288 --> 00:13:22,356
I used to.

218
00:13:22,356 --> 00:13:26,160
It seems there's a lot about Bo Na
that you don't know, Kwon Tae Sung.

219
00:13:28,228 --> 00:13:29,897
Or maybe Bo Na
just doesn't talk about herself?

220
00:13:33,734 --> 00:13:36,336
When we were students,
some of the meaner kids...

221
00:13:36,336 --> 00:13:38,272
used to pick on Bo Na a lot.

222
00:13:38,272 --> 00:13:41,608
They would secretly dip her chicken
in muddy water...

223
00:13:42,576 --> 00:13:45,879
and even mix strong whiskey
into her chicken soup.

224
00:13:46,180 --> 00:13:47,481
So sometimes...

225
00:13:49,116 --> 00:13:50,984
physical fights would break out.

226
00:13:53,086 --> 00:13:55,556
Bo Na was pretty tough back then.

227
00:13:56,190 --> 00:13:57,491
Hey, you really shouldn't...

228
00:13:58,258 --> 00:14:02,596
In Korea, we call that being tough.
Showing no mercy.

229
00:14:03,831 --> 00:14:07,234
Bo Na has strong opinions
and always speaks her mind.

230
00:14:07,234 --> 00:14:08,368
And she has a clear sense
of right and wrong.

231
00:14:08,969 --> 00:14:11,004
Is that so?

232
00:14:11,038 --> 00:14:14,274
Yes, Bo Na enjoys chicken now.
And she likes chicken porridge too.

233
00:14:15,175 --> 00:14:17,911
You know, with food,
it's about who you eat with...

234
00:14:17,945 --> 00:14:22,850
and the memories attached to it.
That can change your tastes, right?

235
00:14:22,883 --> 00:14:24,852
Oh, I see.

236
00:14:24,885 --> 00:14:27,087
I may not have known Bo Na
when she was younger,

237
00:14:27,121 --> 00:14:28,355
but I know her well now.

238
00:14:29,556 --> 00:14:32,259
After all, what's important
is the present, not the past.

239
00:14:33,594 --> 00:14:34,595
Right?

240
00:14:36,663 --> 00:14:39,399
I was wondering what kind of man
Bo Na ended up with,

241
00:14:40,634 --> 00:14:42,269
and it seems she found a good one.

242
00:14:42,302 --> 00:14:45,172
Oh, I'm the one who married
a wonderful woman.

243
00:14:50,210 --> 00:14:51,645
He's tired.

244
00:14:51,645 --> 00:14:53,947
Let's eat up so we can
go grab some tea, okay?

245
00:14:55,249 --> 00:14:56,250
Okay.

246
00:15:04,558 --> 00:15:06,059
We'll just grab a quick cup of tea
and be right back.

247
00:15:06,059 --> 00:15:07,961
Mommy will be right back, Yul. Okay?

248
00:15:07,995 --> 00:15:10,264
Take your time.
You two must have a lot to catch up on...

249
00:15:10,264 --> 00:15:11,298
since it's been a while.

250
00:15:11,331 --> 00:15:13,233
Not really.

251
00:15:13,233 --> 00:15:15,669
Thank you for the delicious chicken
and the lovely conversation.

252
00:15:15,669 --> 00:15:16,703
Hope to see you again.

253
00:15:16,737 --> 00:15:17,871
Okay.

254
00:15:21,208 --> 00:15:22,776
Goodbye, little Yul.

255
00:15:23,477 --> 00:15:24,545
Goodbye.

256
00:15:28,782 --> 00:15:30,584
Goodbye, Tae Sung.

257
00:16:13,327 --> 00:16:14,828
Bo Na.

258
00:16:14,862 --> 00:16:16,296
Calm down.

259
00:16:16,296 --> 00:16:18,031
I told you never to show up
in front of me again.

260
00:16:19,666 --> 00:16:20,667
Just as I thought.

261
00:16:21,368 --> 00:16:23,003
So they're your Achilles' heel,
aren't they?

262
00:16:25,105 --> 00:16:27,541
I guess my warning wasn't strong enough,
was it?

263
00:16:29,042 --> 00:16:30,511
Having something to protect...

264
00:16:31,345 --> 00:16:33,647
is a fatal weakness for killers like us.

265
00:16:41,655 --> 00:16:42,656
Okay.

266
00:16:42,689 --> 00:16:44,491
I won't show up again.

267
00:16:45,559 --> 00:16:46,693
I promise.

268
00:16:47,728 --> 00:16:49,129
This is your second warning.

269
00:16:50,297 --> 00:16:51,298
There won't be a third.

270
00:16:53,834 --> 00:16:54,835
Get lost.

271
00:16:56,503 --> 00:16:58,005
I meant what I said.

272
00:17:02,576 --> 00:17:04,578
That you seem to have found a good man.

273
00:17:43,750 --> 00:17:45,119
No way.

274
00:17:45,119 --> 00:17:47,421
Apparently, Yeon Chang Bok
escaped the hospital during treatment.

275
00:17:48,288 --> 00:17:49,289
Yeon Chang Bok?

276
00:17:50,324 --> 00:17:51,792
Yeon Chang Bok...

277
00:17:53,660 --> 00:17:54,661
Oh, right.

278
00:17:55,162 --> 00:17:56,997
The one who broke into a home
with a weapon...

279
00:17:56,997 --> 00:17:58,766
and committed aggravated sexual assault.

280
00:17:58,766 --> 00:18:00,067
He's human trash.

281
00:18:00,567 --> 00:18:03,604
He held the knife not to the victim,
but to the victim's baby.

282
00:18:03,604 --> 00:18:05,472
The mother ended up killing herself
a few months later.

283
00:18:06,006 --> 00:18:08,475
Right, you covered that case too,
didn't you?

284
00:18:08,475 --> 00:18:09,476
Yes, for a day.

285
00:18:09,476 --> 00:18:13,147
The day Yeon Chang Bok's mother
was pleading for leniency for her son...

286
00:18:13,147 --> 00:18:14,948
during a one-person protest
in front of the courthouse.

287
00:18:14,948 --> 00:18:18,018
That's right.
I went home with the mother...

288
00:18:18,018 --> 00:18:19,386
and saw Yeon Chang Bok's son.

289
00:18:19,953 --> 00:18:22,723
Someone like that should be killed
by Kingfisher.

290
00:18:24,324 --> 00:18:26,260
Are you a fan of Kingfisher, Reporter Nam?

291
00:18:26,293 --> 00:18:28,962
Oh, plenty of reporters
secretly support Kingfisher.

292
00:18:29,730 --> 00:18:31,231
Wait a minute.

293
00:18:31,265 --> 00:18:33,667
At this rate, what if Kingfisher
gets to that bastard first?

294
00:18:34,168 --> 00:18:36,303
They're always one step ahead
of the police, you know.

295
00:18:37,571 --> 00:18:39,706
Honestly, rather than him being caught
by the police,

296
00:18:39,706 --> 00:18:40,707
that might be for the best.

297
00:18:41,208 --> 00:18:42,242
Reporter Nam, I'm sorry,

298
00:18:42,276 --> 00:18:43,644
but you'll have to go back
to the office alone.

299
00:18:44,144 --> 00:18:45,813
What? Why?

300
00:19:17,478 --> 00:19:20,114
(Fiercely Oppose Redevelopment.
Demand Fair Compensation.)

301
00:19:24,017 --> 00:19:27,121
(Demolition)

302
00:19:29,823 --> 00:19:31,391
(Private)

303
00:19:37,564 --> 00:19:39,333
(Haegong Gosiwon)

304
00:20:49,837 --> 00:20:52,840
Hey, reckless young man.

305
00:20:53,240 --> 00:20:57,578
You should know that in this world,
some doors...

306
00:20:58,045 --> 00:20:59,680
are best left unopened.

307
00:21:02,116 --> 00:21:05,152
Surprise. Hello, comrade.

308
00:21:09,556 --> 00:21:10,891
I'm cutting comms for a moment.

309
00:21:12,092 --> 00:21:13,160
What are you doing here?

310
00:21:13,494 --> 00:21:14,928
Why are you...

311
00:21:16,063 --> 00:21:17,264
How did you know I was here?

312
00:21:26,173 --> 00:21:27,808
You still have sticky fingers, I see.

313
00:21:29,810 --> 00:21:31,145
So, is something wrong?

314
00:21:31,145 --> 00:21:33,313
Letting your guard down?
That's not like you, Yu Bo Na.

315
00:21:34,414 --> 00:21:36,950
- What brings you to Korea?
- Well, I was bored, so I came to play.

316
00:21:37,651 --> 00:21:40,487
Russia is so boring without Bo Na.

317
00:21:40,487 --> 00:21:41,488
Go away. I'm working.

318
00:21:44,191 --> 00:21:45,359
No, but...

319
00:21:45,626 --> 00:21:46,760
Did something go wrong?

320
00:21:46,760 --> 00:21:49,029
The Client has a visitor,
so I'm on standby.

321
00:21:54,802 --> 00:21:56,003
Now that sounds like Yu Bo Na.

322
00:21:57,070 --> 00:21:58,372
But when the guest leaves,

323
00:21:59,106 --> 00:22:00,107
can you do it then?

324
00:22:00,741 --> 00:22:02,142
Since it's still the early stages,

325
00:22:02,176 --> 00:22:04,344
didn't they say
you have to be extra careful?

326
00:22:07,214 --> 00:22:08,849
How much do you... No...

327
00:22:10,317 --> 00:22:11,585
Isn't this a time when...

328
00:22:12,052 --> 00:22:14,488
you should only be looking at
beautiful things?

329
00:22:16,790 --> 00:22:18,592
Still, if you absolutely have to do it,

330
00:22:19,393 --> 00:22:21,094
how about hiring a mercenary?

331
00:22:28,102 --> 00:22:29,303
A mercenary?

332
00:22:29,970 --> 00:22:31,305
The best mercenary.

333
00:22:40,314 --> 00:22:42,683
Then just pull the trigger.
I'll do the rest.

334
00:22:44,485 --> 00:22:45,486
A wise choice.

335
00:22:46,453 --> 00:22:47,721
Not yet. Wait.

336
00:22:49,223 --> 00:22:51,191
Come on, I have to confirm the location.

337
00:23:03,937 --> 00:23:05,939
Is there just one guest?

338
00:23:08,842 --> 00:23:09,977
Yes.

339
00:23:11,445 --> 00:23:12,546
It's a young boy?

340
00:23:12,880 --> 00:23:15,582
His son.
Once you confirm the child is leaving,

341
00:23:15,582 --> 00:23:16,583
take the shot then.

342
00:23:17,818 --> 00:23:19,887
- Done.
- What do you think you're doing?

343
00:23:27,861 --> 00:23:30,431
Calm down, Bo Na.

344
00:23:30,831 --> 00:23:33,567
You crazy bastard.
Do you have a death wish?

345
00:23:34,501 --> 00:23:38,539
When to pull the trigger
is decided by the one holding the gun.

346
00:23:39,106 --> 00:23:41,208
- You know that.
- The son is innocent.

347
00:23:42,209 --> 00:23:43,243
He's an innocent child.

348
00:23:43,744 --> 00:23:45,479
Your name...

349
00:23:45,979 --> 00:23:49,216
is on your tombstone when you die.

350
00:23:49,716 --> 00:23:51,051
Your sins...

351
00:23:51,051 --> 00:23:55,155
pass on to your children
even after you die.

352
00:23:56,089 --> 00:23:57,791
That's what Mama always used to say.

353
00:23:57,825 --> 00:23:59,126
Shut up, you bastard.

354
00:24:08,135 --> 00:24:10,104
Hey, it's not like I killed the kid
like someone we know, right?

355
00:24:10,704 --> 00:24:11,805
I didn't kill him.

356
00:24:12,806 --> 00:24:14,074
Isn't that what matters?

357
00:24:16,210 --> 00:24:17,511
Bo Na.

358
00:24:17,511 --> 00:24:19,480
The doctor said that
stress is not good for the baby...

359
00:24:52,946 --> 00:24:54,448
(Kwon Tae Sung,
Social Affairs Desk Reporter)

360
00:24:54,448 --> 00:24:55,849
Kwon Tae Sung.

361
00:24:57,918 --> 00:24:58,919
So he's a reporter.

362
00:25:01,155 --> 00:25:02,156
What is this?

363
00:25:07,294 --> 00:25:08,362
Interesting.

364
00:25:37,024 --> 00:25:38,025
You're awake.

365
00:25:40,427 --> 00:25:41,428
Reporter Kwon Tae Sung.

366
00:25:42,796 --> 00:25:43,797
About what happened today...

367
00:25:45,032 --> 00:25:46,834
You should erase it from your mind.

368
00:25:48,435 --> 00:25:50,037
And from now on, regarding Kingfisher,

369
00:25:50,904 --> 00:25:52,339
it's best you lose interest.

370
00:25:55,409 --> 00:25:57,044
If you break this promise,

371
00:25:59,079 --> 00:26:00,681
your wife,

372
00:26:01,215 --> 00:26:02,216
and your child,

373
00:26:02,649 --> 00:26:04,485
your family could be in danger.

374
00:26:15,829 --> 00:26:17,498
As long as you keep this promise,

375
00:26:18,432 --> 00:26:19,633
nothing will happen.

376
00:26:21,869 --> 00:26:23,303
Now, then...

377
00:26:29,710 --> 00:26:31,378
Good night, Tae Sung.

378
00:26:38,118 --> 00:26:41,088
Why is Yu Bo Na still so angry?

379
00:26:41,922 --> 00:26:45,092
Did I leave a scratch
on the flawless history...

380
00:26:45,526 --> 00:26:46,560
of Kingfisher?

381
00:26:46,994 --> 00:26:49,997
You left a child with a scar
they'll carry for the rest of their life.

382
00:26:51,665 --> 00:26:54,668
Did I forcibly take the gun?

383
00:26:54,701 --> 00:26:58,238
You were the one who made the choice.
To protect something,

384
00:26:58,238 --> 00:27:00,240
don't you have to give something else up?

385
00:27:01,675 --> 00:27:02,810
You're wrong.

386
00:27:03,677 --> 00:27:05,612
It wasn't a sacrifice. It was a mistake.

387
00:27:06,547 --> 00:27:07,881
My mistake was trusting
you for a moment...

388
00:27:08,615 --> 00:27:10,984
and forgetting what a bastard you are.

389
00:27:12,953 --> 00:27:13,987
Go back while you're still alive.

390
00:27:16,423 --> 00:27:17,458
Aren't you going to ask me this time?

391
00:27:17,858 --> 00:27:19,226
What brings me to Korea?

392
00:27:21,228 --> 00:27:22,396
Just keep your promise.

393
00:27:23,397 --> 00:27:24,498
This is your last warning.

394
00:27:29,937 --> 00:27:31,438
Oh, I'll keep my promise.

395
00:27:32,639 --> 00:27:35,109
After all, you'll be the one
to come looking for me.

396
00:27:37,411 --> 00:27:38,645
When that happens,

397
00:27:39,546 --> 00:27:42,449
what choice will you make, Yu Bo Na?

398
00:27:49,323 --> 00:27:50,724
(You keep your promise. Good boy.
Good night, Tae Sung.)

399
00:27:52,693 --> 00:27:54,294
Good night, Tae Sung.

400
00:27:54,995 --> 00:27:56,563
Goodbye, Tae Sung.

401
00:27:57,765 --> 00:27:59,066
(You keep your promise. Good boy.
Good night, Tae Sung.)

402
00:28:14,047 --> 00:28:16,216
(Detective Lee Dong Jin)

403
00:28:24,391 --> 00:28:25,492
Why did you call me to a place...

404
00:28:26,293 --> 00:28:27,394
so secluded?

405
00:28:34,668 --> 00:28:35,869
Are you Kingfisher?

406
00:28:38,739 --> 00:28:40,841
Are you seriously asking me that?

407
00:28:40,874 --> 00:28:42,609
The World Cup and Haegong-dong.

408
00:28:42,609 --> 00:28:45,279
You were at the scene
of both major incidents.

409
00:28:45,312 --> 00:28:46,613
The odds of that are impossible.

410
00:28:47,214 --> 00:28:48,315
Are you still drunk?

411
00:28:48,849 --> 00:28:50,918
I'm a reporter, you psycho.

412
00:28:50,918 --> 00:28:51,919
Tell me.

413
00:28:51,952 --> 00:28:54,087
Everything that happened that day.
I'm not kidding.

414
00:28:59,760 --> 00:29:03,097
The seven-year-old boy
who was at the Haegong-dong scene.

415
00:29:04,531 --> 00:29:06,767
What? Where did that come from?

416
00:29:06,800 --> 00:29:08,969
Since I never heard about it,
you must have kept it from the press...

417
00:29:08,969 --> 00:29:10,037
to protect him.

418
00:29:10,070 --> 00:29:11,572
That's right. So?

419
00:29:11,605 --> 00:29:12,840
Me too.

420
00:29:13,240 --> 00:29:14,408
I'm under an embargo too.

421
00:29:18,312 --> 00:29:19,513
What?

422
00:29:22,182 --> 00:29:23,951
I have to protect someone too.

423
00:29:29,723 --> 00:29:30,724
Let me ask you one thing.

424
00:29:31,492 --> 00:29:33,127
The man you said you saw that day...

425
00:29:34,128 --> 00:29:35,162
Are you sure it was Kingfisher?

426
00:29:39,633 --> 00:29:41,001
What about you?

427
00:29:41,001 --> 00:29:43,804
Are you sure Kingfisher shot him that day,
knowing he had a son?

428
00:29:50,611 --> 00:29:51,879
I already heard.

429
00:29:52,546 --> 00:29:53,947
I can't unhear it.

430
00:29:54,782 --> 00:29:57,818
If that man really is Kingfisher,
you're a witness,

431
00:29:57,818 --> 00:30:00,120
but if not, this could derail
the investigation. Do you understand?

432
00:30:02,289 --> 00:30:04,224
- I know.
- I can't wait long.

433
00:30:05,025 --> 00:30:06,593
Whatever the reason,
sort it out and tell me.

434
00:30:06,627 --> 00:30:08,028
Or I'll force a confession out of you.

435
00:30:10,164 --> 00:30:11,165
Got it?

436
00:30:11,832 --> 00:30:12,933
Goodness.

437
00:30:23,744 --> 00:30:25,345
Your wife...

438
00:30:26,113 --> 00:30:27,114
and your child,

439
00:30:28,515 --> 00:30:30,350
your family could be in danger.

440
00:30:30,384 --> 00:30:34,788
(4 Years Ago, "That" Night)

441
00:30:39,660 --> 00:30:40,861
Honey, what's wrong?

442
00:30:41,495 --> 00:30:44,298
- What?
- You're barely eating. Something wrong?

443
00:30:45,265 --> 00:30:46,266
No.

444
00:30:47,434 --> 00:30:48,435
Nothing's wrong.

445
00:30:50,604 --> 00:30:51,605
This is delicious.

446
00:30:54,108 --> 00:30:56,310
Didn't you say you had
something to show me?

447
00:30:57,244 --> 00:30:59,146
- Yes.
- What is it?

448
00:31:03,851 --> 00:31:05,185
What is it?

449
00:31:05,452 --> 00:31:06,453
Look at this.

450
00:31:08,322 --> 00:31:09,323
What is this?

451
00:31:19,399 --> 00:31:21,869
I went to the doctor today and...

452
00:31:28,609 --> 00:31:29,610
<i>Thank goodness...</i>

453
00:31:31,011 --> 00:31:32,079
<i>I made it back.</i>

454
00:31:34,148 --> 00:31:35,282
Tae Sung.

455
00:31:38,252 --> 00:31:39,286
Honey, are you crying?

456
00:31:39,887 --> 00:31:41,121
I'm not crying.

457
00:31:42,189 --> 00:31:43,223
<i>To Bo Na...</i>

458
00:31:44,725 --> 00:31:46,593
<i>To our child...</i>

459
00:31:47,761 --> 00:31:48,829
<i>I'm so relieved.</i>

460
00:31:50,464 --> 00:31:51,899
Are you crying again?

461
00:31:52,299 --> 00:31:53,300
Are you a crybaby?

462
00:31:53,333 --> 00:31:55,836
No, I'm not crying.
I'm just happy, that's all.

463
00:31:56,603 --> 00:31:59,239
Even I'm not crying, so why are you?

464
00:32:10,217 --> 00:32:12,352
Look at this. This is our baby.

465
00:32:31,371 --> 00:32:33,574
Hey. It's orange.

466
00:32:34,041 --> 00:32:35,609
What color is this?

467
00:32:36,443 --> 00:32:38,245
What's inside the orange one?

468
00:32:38,278 --> 00:32:42,149
Ta-da. Wow, it's green, right?

469
00:32:42,749 --> 00:32:43,750
This is in here too...

470
00:32:43,750 --> 00:32:45,486
<i>So those two are your Achilles' heel.</i>

471
00:32:45,886 --> 00:32:47,654
Having something to protect...

472
00:32:48,355 --> 00:32:50,958
For killers like us,
that's a fatal weakness.

473
00:32:53,393 --> 00:32:54,862
It's blue.

474
00:32:58,665 --> 00:33:00,300
- Mom, what is it?
- What?

475
00:33:00,300 --> 00:33:04,538
- Mom, what's wrong?
- Me? I'm just recharging my happiness.

476
00:33:05,305 --> 00:33:08,442
When I hug you like this, Yul,
my happiness recharges.

477
00:33:09,510 --> 00:33:11,311
I'm recharging my happiness too.

478
00:33:11,311 --> 00:33:12,379
You too?

479
00:33:27,791 --> 00:33:29,960
(Durumi Electronics)

480
00:33:31,937 --> 00:33:35,807
- Returning this. Thanks.
- Just this one? Where are the others?

481
00:33:35,807 --> 00:33:37,009
I sent them somewhere.

482
00:33:38,010 --> 00:33:39,678
Don't file an expense report.
Just bill me.

483
00:33:51,023 --> 00:33:52,024
Gwangjang Market.

484
00:33:52,557 --> 00:33:53,925
Guess he was craving their pancakes?

485
00:33:54,359 --> 00:33:55,560
Well, look who it is.

486
00:33:55,994 --> 00:33:57,062
Is he tracking down good restaurants?

487
00:33:57,095 --> 00:33:59,498
It didn't seem like
he was just on a food tour.

488
00:33:59,498 --> 00:34:00,565
Share this with me.

489
00:34:08,807 --> 00:34:10,609
Gosh, that looks delicious.

490
00:34:15,347 --> 00:34:16,348
They're not here.

491
00:34:16,381 --> 00:34:18,116
They must've left already.

492
00:34:18,116 --> 00:34:20,652
It seems that Bo Na doesn't know it yet.

493
00:34:24,222 --> 00:34:25,257
Me?

494
00:34:25,857 --> 00:34:30,329
Since I'm here, I'll look for a nice place
to eat around here.

495
00:34:30,829 --> 00:34:32,931
There are many great restaurants in Korea.

496
00:34:32,965 --> 00:34:34,866
(Sergei Volansky, Sergei Volkov,
Russian Anthropologist)

497
00:34:36,234 --> 00:34:37,235
Senior Kwon.

498
00:34:39,371 --> 00:34:40,472
Senior Kwon?

499
00:34:41,139 --> 00:34:42,441
Yes.

500
00:34:42,474 --> 00:34:45,577
You were so lost in thought.
You didn't hear me calling you?

501
00:34:47,746 --> 00:34:50,816
If I heard a voice for the first time
four years ago,

502
00:34:50,816 --> 00:34:52,918
do you think I'd recognize it
if I heard it again now?

503
00:34:55,220 --> 00:34:57,356
I don't know.

504
00:34:57,356 --> 00:35:00,459
Well, maybe if it was a voice
you heard often,

505
00:35:00,459 --> 00:35:02,160
like a singer or an actor,
then it might be possible.

506
00:35:03,629 --> 00:35:05,330
But it'd be hard to remember
after hearing it once, right?

507
00:35:05,931 --> 00:35:07,666
But why do you ask?

508
00:35:08,967 --> 00:35:09,968
It's nothing.

509
00:35:11,970 --> 00:35:13,038
Let's start the meeting.

510
00:35:14,306 --> 00:35:16,408
Have you figured out
how many of the parolees...

511
00:35:16,408 --> 00:35:17,409
are violent offenders?

512
00:35:18,610 --> 00:35:21,780
I received and analyzed data
from the last ten years.

513
00:35:21,813 --> 00:35:24,349
I've organized them by the type
of violent crime,

514
00:35:24,349 --> 00:35:26,485
such as murder, drugs, or sexual assault.

515
00:35:27,052 --> 00:35:29,655
And this is a separate list
of just the violent offenders...

516
00:35:29,688 --> 00:35:30,822
released this year.

517
00:35:32,691 --> 00:35:34,559
You must have worked hard on this.

518
00:35:36,395 --> 00:35:37,396
(2026 Parolees: Violent Offenders)

519
00:35:39,131 --> 00:35:40,532
(Jang Eun Hak: Manslaughter)

520
00:35:43,769 --> 00:35:45,804
Senior Kwon, what is it?

521
00:35:48,407 --> 00:35:52,010
(Jang Eun Hak: Manslaughter,
2007, Seoul, Model Prisoner)

522
00:36:06,792 --> 00:36:08,961
<i>Can you be certain that</i>
<i>Kingfisher shot him...</i>

523
00:36:08,961 --> 00:36:10,896
<i>knowing his son was there?</i>

524
00:36:16,335 --> 00:36:17,336
Sir.

525
00:36:18,704 --> 00:36:20,806
I got the victim's statement
from the couple assault case.

526
00:36:20,806 --> 00:36:22,674
What should I do?
Should I send a request to the Cyber Team?

527
00:36:22,708 --> 00:36:24,977
Do it. Let me know if you find anything.

528
00:36:25,010 --> 00:36:26,044
Yes, sir.

529
00:36:29,848 --> 00:36:31,049
Hey, what have you been so focused on?

530
00:36:33,185 --> 00:36:35,320
The Haegong-dong <i>gosiwon?</i> What's this for?

531
00:36:37,422 --> 00:36:38,423
Why aren't you asking me?

532
00:36:38,457 --> 00:36:39,558
About what?

533
00:36:40,559 --> 00:36:42,928
About killing him in front of his son.

534
00:36:42,928 --> 00:36:44,830
That's just speculation, isn't it?

535
00:36:45,564 --> 00:36:47,165
To be honest, I don't think Kingfisher...

536
00:36:47,165 --> 00:36:49,401
would have pulled the trigger
knowing a child was there.

537
00:36:50,068 --> 00:36:51,703
Here, look.

538
00:36:52,204 --> 00:36:53,705
The <i>gosiwon's</i> window is small.

539
00:36:53,739 --> 00:36:57,242
From the sniper's vantage point,
there could have been a blind spot, right?

540
00:37:02,948 --> 00:37:05,717
Beom, go home early today.

541
00:37:06,218 --> 00:37:08,387
Go home?

542
00:37:09,421 --> 00:37:10,822
Are you telling me to go home now?

543
00:37:10,822 --> 00:37:11,923
Not work late?

544
00:37:12,791 --> 00:37:14,293
You want to work late then?

545
00:37:15,327 --> 00:37:16,495
For real?

546
00:37:19,598 --> 00:37:21,133
No take-backs.

547
00:37:21,133 --> 00:37:23,702
Then I'll just stop by the Cyber Team
and head straight home.

548
00:37:26,071 --> 00:37:27,072
Yes, sir.

549
00:37:29,141 --> 00:37:30,909
- Hey, where are you going?
- Home! I'm going home!

550
00:37:32,477 --> 00:37:33,545
(Incoming Call: Reporter Kwon Tae Sung)

551
00:37:35,247 --> 00:37:36,515
Is the embargo over already?

552
00:37:38,517 --> 00:37:40,319
You called, so talk. What is it?

553
00:37:41,053 --> 00:37:44,756
- Dong Jin.
- Why so sweetly? Makes me nervous.

554
00:37:45,691 --> 00:37:46,825
Why? What's going on?

555
00:37:48,794 --> 00:37:50,095
That bastard was released.

556
00:37:50,128 --> 00:37:52,230
That bastard? Which bastard?

557
00:37:53,231 --> 00:37:54,566
On parole, a month ago.

558
00:37:58,537 --> 00:37:59,605
What?

559
00:38:02,708 --> 00:38:05,944
<i>Also known as</i>
<i>the Gammyeon-dong Supermarket Murder Case.</i>

560
00:38:07,112 --> 00:38:09,881
The culprit, Jang Eun Hak,
used a broken soju bottle...

561
00:38:09,881 --> 00:38:10,983
at a neighborhood supermarket...

562
00:38:10,983 --> 00:38:14,920
to brutally murder the two owners,
a married couple, and fled the scene.

563
00:38:14,953 --> 00:38:18,423
He was caught 4 years later
and sentenced to 16 years...

564
00:38:18,790 --> 00:38:22,594
but was paroled last month
with one year left on his sentence.

565
00:38:23,095 --> 00:38:25,631
- Hello, sir.
- Yes. Hello.

566
00:38:25,631 --> 00:38:26,698
Hello.

567
00:38:27,366 --> 00:38:29,368
- Are you looking for a bed?
- Yes, a bed.

568
00:38:29,368 --> 00:38:30,836
What size are you looking for?

569
00:38:36,975 --> 00:38:38,143
Jang.

570
00:38:39,211 --> 00:38:40,512
Jang!

571
00:38:40,512 --> 00:38:42,514
- Yes.
- Clean that up.

572
00:38:43,415 --> 00:38:44,650
Yes, sir.

573
00:38:47,419 --> 00:38:48,920
Goodness.

574
00:38:50,822 --> 00:38:54,259
He brutally killed 2 people
and only got 16 years?

575
00:38:54,860 --> 00:38:55,961
What is this?

576
00:38:55,961 --> 00:38:59,131
He was convicted of
involuntary manslaughter, not murder.

577
00:38:59,131 --> 00:39:00,198
That's right.

578
00:39:00,198 --> 00:39:04,369
He committed the crime during an argument
because he was short ten cents for soju,

579
00:39:04,369 --> 00:39:06,772
and in court, he claimed he was drunk...

580
00:39:06,772 --> 00:39:11,843
and felt humiliated when he did it.
He basically pleaded with the court.

581
00:39:11,877 --> 00:39:14,746
He exploited the leniency of the law.
The "justice can be compassionate" thing.

582
00:39:15,781 --> 00:39:17,916
Meanwhile, the victims' families
are shedding tears of blood.

583
00:39:19,084 --> 00:39:20,352
Shedding tears of blood, yes.

584
00:39:21,453 --> 00:39:22,554
The kind that will never dry.

585
00:39:26,391 --> 00:39:30,362
But there's one peculiar detail here.

586
00:39:31,997 --> 00:39:35,267
<i>The victims' family has a son,</i>

587
00:39:36,268 --> 00:39:39,271
<i>and this son is a detective.</i>

588
00:39:40,839 --> 00:39:46,044
What's even stranger is that
he once worked the Kingfisher case.

589
00:39:48,146 --> 00:39:50,082
Wow, that's really ironic.

590
00:39:50,515 --> 00:39:53,919
So a victim's family member is a cop
chasing Kingfisher.

591
00:39:54,419 --> 00:39:56,989
If he finds out the killer was paroled
on top of that sentence,

592
00:39:56,989 --> 00:39:58,490
he'll be devastated.

593
00:39:58,490 --> 00:40:00,058
Not devastation. Rage.

594
00:40:01,927 --> 00:40:04,262
Do you think he might
do something dangerous?

595
00:40:04,296 --> 00:40:07,566
I wonder. He's a cop, so he has a gun.

596
00:40:09,334 --> 00:40:10,602
No, he's not that kind of person.

597
00:40:12,170 --> 00:40:15,240
If he wanted personal revenge,
he wouldn't have become a cop.

598
00:40:15,841 --> 00:40:19,011
It's about making criminals pay
within the bounds of the law.

599
00:40:19,011 --> 00:40:20,078
That's what police do.

600
00:40:23,548 --> 00:40:24,883
(The Bereaved: Lee Dong Jin,
17 at the time of the incident)

601
00:40:40,299 --> 00:40:42,935
A date, Se Ah?

602
00:40:42,968 --> 00:40:44,102
Just the two of us?

603
00:40:45,904 --> 00:40:48,407
Really? Where should we meet then?

604
00:40:48,440 --> 00:40:50,375
She wants to meet up.
Just the two of them?

605
00:40:50,375 --> 00:40:52,778
That has "sister-in-law summons"
written all over it.

606
00:40:53,245 --> 00:40:56,214
Still, isn't a sister-in-law
easier to deal with than a mother-in-law?

607
00:40:56,214 --> 00:40:58,917
They say "a meddling sister-in-law
is the worst" for a reason.

608
00:40:59,484 --> 00:41:00,686
Someone's in trouble.

609
00:41:01,453 --> 00:41:03,121
Or is about to be.

610
00:41:16,201 --> 00:41:18,670
If you find anything,
please contact me right away. Sir.

611
00:41:20,672 --> 00:41:24,776
(Cyber Investigation 911 Dispatch)

612
00:41:26,912 --> 00:41:28,847
<i>I'm getting off on time</i>
<i>for the first time in forever.</i>

613
00:41:29,781 --> 00:41:30,816
Want to hit the gaming cafe?

614
00:41:31,383 --> 00:41:33,185
<i>Nope. Got a date.</i>

615
00:41:33,185 --> 00:41:34,219
A date?

616
00:41:36,154 --> 00:41:37,155
With a guy?

617
00:41:37,189 --> 00:41:38,390
<i>With my sister-in-law.</i>

618
00:41:39,691 --> 00:41:40,959
Of course.

619
00:41:43,695 --> 00:41:45,998
Gosh, what should I do then?

620
00:41:47,165 --> 00:41:50,636
Hey, over here.
They say this place is really good.

621
00:41:50,636 --> 00:41:52,237
- Looks like there's no line today.
- It's so pretty.

622
00:41:52,738 --> 00:41:54,473
- Welcome.
- A table for two, please.

623
00:41:54,473 --> 00:41:56,041
- Do you have a reservation?
- No.

624
00:41:56,041 --> 00:41:58,710
You have to make a reservation
through our app first.

625
00:41:58,744 --> 00:42:01,113
- Through the app?
- Yes, I'm sorry.

626
00:42:01,113 --> 00:42:03,415
Would you like to wait?

627
00:42:03,415 --> 00:42:04,483
Wait...

628
00:42:04,483 --> 00:42:06,018
(Name, Party Size)

629
00:42:06,051 --> 00:42:07,719
- There must be 20 people ahead of us.
- Party number 285.

630
00:42:07,719 --> 00:42:09,721
- What should we do?
- This way, please.

631
00:42:11,857 --> 00:42:13,859
- Thank you.
- Enjoy your meal.

632
00:42:13,892 --> 00:42:16,828
- Like this and...
- Hey, wait a minute.

633
00:42:16,828 --> 00:42:18,130
No? Not yet?

634
00:42:24,436 --> 00:42:26,338
Hey, should we take a picture
together too?

635
00:42:26,371 --> 00:42:27,539
Sure.

636
00:42:29,341 --> 00:42:30,842
Don't look at the camera.

637
00:42:30,842 --> 00:42:32,044
Yes, pretend you're busy
and not looking.

638
00:42:32,077 --> 00:42:33,445
And look your cutest.

639
00:42:33,478 --> 00:42:35,614
Cute.

640
00:42:35,647 --> 00:42:38,784
- It's so cute.
- Ta-da. What do you think?

641
00:42:38,784 --> 00:42:40,752
Oh my, you look like a rabbit.
Is it for both of us?

642
00:42:40,786 --> 00:42:41,954
- Heart.
- Heart.

643
00:42:46,925 --> 00:42:49,861
You're so strange sometimes, Mom.

644
00:42:50,295 --> 00:42:51,964
You give her such a hard time,

645
00:42:51,964 --> 00:42:54,333
but you always bring her
all these side dishes.

646
00:42:54,333 --> 00:42:57,202
I don't bring them for her.

647
00:42:57,235 --> 00:42:58,704
Do you think I do it for her?

648
00:42:59,037 --> 00:43:01,139
I do it so my son has something to eat.

649
00:43:01,974 --> 00:43:04,543
Goodness, other mothers-in-law
go out of their way...

650
00:43:04,576 --> 00:43:05,777
to feed their sons-in-law...

651
00:43:05,777 --> 00:43:07,479
and bring them all sorts of food.

652
00:43:07,479 --> 00:43:09,214
There you go again.

653
00:43:09,247 --> 00:43:11,450
- I'm so tired.
- Oh, you're back?

654
00:43:11,483 --> 00:43:13,352
Soon Il, can you get me a glass of water?

655
00:43:13,352 --> 00:43:14,353
Yes, of course.

656
00:43:14,753 --> 00:43:17,990
- Where did you go?
- The department store.

657
00:43:18,023 --> 00:43:19,358
The day after tomorrow,

658
00:43:19,358 --> 00:43:21,159
we have the formal family meeting
with Jun Woo's in-laws.

659
00:43:21,593 --> 00:43:23,829
Oh, you said
your second son's date was set.

660
00:43:24,396 --> 00:43:25,530
But why the department store?

661
00:43:25,530 --> 00:43:27,666
Well, I don't have
anything decent to wear.

662
00:43:28,300 --> 00:43:31,270
Seon Ja, what did you wear
for Tae Sung's family meeting?

663
00:43:31,303 --> 00:43:32,404
Huh?

664
00:43:33,171 --> 00:43:34,906
Oh, just something casual.

665
00:43:35,440 --> 00:43:37,342
Oh, right. You didn't have one, did you?

666
00:43:38,076 --> 00:43:40,178
Wow, that must have been a relief for you.

667
00:43:41,046 --> 00:43:42,547
Oh, my back.

668
00:43:42,547 --> 00:43:44,316
What do you mean I didn't have one?

669
00:43:44,349 --> 00:43:46,551
I've had two of them for my daughters.

670
00:43:47,286 --> 00:43:50,622
Please. Is a meeting for your daughter
the same as one for your son?

671
00:43:52,758 --> 00:43:55,694
A meeting is a meeting.
What's the difference?

672
00:43:56,962 --> 00:44:00,999
You can tell everything about a family
from the parents at those meetings.

673
00:44:00,999 --> 00:44:04,036
My son's future in-laws are both teachers.

674
00:44:05,103 --> 00:44:08,273
And you can tell.
Their daughter is so well-mannered,

675
00:44:08,273 --> 00:44:10,943
and she has such a bright and happy face.

676
00:44:10,943 --> 00:44:13,612
It's obvious she grew up
surrounded by love.

677
00:44:15,447 --> 00:44:18,617
Oh, maybe I shouldn't be saying this
in front of you.

678
00:44:19,384 --> 00:44:21,153
- Since your daughter-in-law is...
- You wench.

679
00:44:21,186 --> 00:44:23,188
- My goodness.
- Hey, what's with you?

680
00:44:23,288 --> 00:44:25,023
Hey, what did I do?

681
00:44:25,023 --> 00:44:28,560
Fine. I didn't have a family meeting,
and I don't have in-laws.

682
00:44:28,593 --> 00:44:30,529
Because my daughter-in-law is an orphan.

683
00:44:30,529 --> 00:44:34,299
So what? What about it?
Did you contribute a single penny?

684
00:44:34,299 --> 00:44:37,002
Hey, I gave you a generous wedding gift.

685
00:44:37,002 --> 00:44:40,305
Why are you acting so proud of having
an orphan for a daughter-in-law?

686
00:44:40,339 --> 00:44:42,708
And I've been friends with her
my whole life.

687
00:44:43,008 --> 00:44:44,743
You wench. You're going to get it today.

688
00:44:44,743 --> 00:44:46,645
My goodness. Hey!

689
00:44:56,054 --> 00:44:59,191
Se Ah, what do you and your friends
usually do for fun?

690
00:44:59,224 --> 00:45:00,892
- Me?
- Yes.

691
00:45:00,892 --> 00:45:04,630
Well, it's chicken feet and soju
or pork belly and beer.

692
00:45:04,630 --> 00:45:05,998
Mm...

693
00:45:07,299 --> 00:45:09,401
Was I that obvious?

694
00:45:10,602 --> 00:45:13,839
To be honest, I did some research
before we met up.

695
00:45:13,872 --> 00:45:16,174
I was trying to figure out
what young people do for fun these days.

696
00:45:17,276 --> 00:45:19,344
You know, places like that cafe
we went to.

697
00:45:19,811 --> 00:45:24,049
It's not really my kind of thing,
but I thought you might like it.

698
00:45:24,516 --> 00:45:25,684
Ah...

699
00:45:25,684 --> 00:45:27,719
So that was your first time.

700
00:45:30,989 --> 00:45:32,958
For me, just sitting here
with you like this,

701
00:45:32,958 --> 00:45:35,527
just doing nothing is
more than enough for me.

702
00:45:37,296 --> 00:45:39,398
- Really?
- Yes.

703
00:45:42,634 --> 00:45:45,904
Then where's the one place
you go to all the time?

704
00:45:45,904 --> 00:45:47,472
Let's make that our last stop.

705
00:45:47,506 --> 00:45:49,207
- Really?
- Yes.

706
00:45:49,241 --> 00:45:52,477
Well, there is this one place...

707
00:45:56,415 --> 00:45:57,482
(New Message From Se Dol)

708
00:46:01,920 --> 00:46:03,488
<i>Bon PC Cafe.</i>

709
00:46:03,522 --> 00:46:04,790
<i>Get over here right now.</i>

710
00:46:11,830 --> 00:46:14,399
Hey, what took you so long?
I thought you were getting off on time.

711
00:46:16,635 --> 00:46:18,337
Hey, I was hanging out
somewhere else first.

712
00:46:18,370 --> 00:46:20,138
You think you're my only friend?

713
00:46:21,039 --> 00:46:24,643
Hey, say hi. This is my sister-in-law.
Bo Na, this is my friend, Horangi.

714
00:46:24,643 --> 00:46:26,511
- Hello.
- Hi.

715
00:46:26,511 --> 00:46:29,848
So your friend is a guy, Se Ah.
Is he your boyfriend?

716
00:46:29,848 --> 00:46:32,017
No. We're just friends, Bo Na.

717
00:46:32,017 --> 00:46:33,952
Sister-in-law,
let me formally introduce myself.

718
00:46:33,986 --> 00:46:35,320
I'm Beom Sung Hoon.

719
00:46:35,320 --> 00:46:37,956
I'm very sorry
I couldn't make it to the wedding.

720
00:46:37,990 --> 00:46:39,691
Oh, no. It's fine.

721
00:46:40,592 --> 00:46:42,160
He's handsome.

722
00:46:44,029 --> 00:46:46,465
All right, that's enough of
the formal introductions. Sit over there.

723
00:46:46,465 --> 00:46:49,167
All right, your mission today is...

724
00:46:49,167 --> 00:46:52,938
to show my sister-in-law
the sweet taste of victory. Got it?

725
00:46:53,438 --> 00:46:55,807
My shoulders feel a bit heavy.

726
00:46:55,807 --> 00:46:57,342
I'm counting on you.

727
00:46:58,010 --> 00:47:02,047
Since my friend is here,
would you like to try an FPS game?

728
00:47:02,080 --> 00:47:05,183
- FPS?
- Yes, when you're really stressed,

729
00:47:05,183 --> 00:47:07,052
a shooter game is the best.

730
00:47:09,454 --> 00:47:10,856
You know, sniping.

731
00:47:11,523 --> 00:47:13,325
There's a game where you snipe?

732
00:47:13,358 --> 00:47:14,893
Yes.

733
00:47:14,893 --> 00:47:19,531
It's a little difficult,
but you can just follow us.

734
00:47:19,531 --> 00:47:22,534
He'll do all the killing anyway.

735
00:47:23,135 --> 00:47:24,136
I'm counting on you.

736
00:47:24,169 --> 00:47:27,172
I'm not that good.

737
00:47:27,873 --> 00:47:30,409
- Okay. Shall we give it a go then?
- Okay.

738
00:47:34,379 --> 00:47:36,315
Over there, there, there.
I got one.

739
00:47:36,315 --> 00:47:38,583
- Over there, in the SW direction.
- Okay. Roger.

740
00:47:38,617 --> 00:47:41,787
- Nice.
- It's nothing.

741
00:47:41,787 --> 00:47:43,021
Hey, be careful. There's one more.

742
00:47:43,021 --> 00:47:44,756
Hey, over there, behind that wall.

743
00:47:44,790 --> 00:47:46,725
- I hit one.
- Gosh, what's gotten into you?

744
00:47:47,492 --> 00:47:50,862
- Ping number 1.
- Yes, assist.

745
00:47:50,896 --> 00:47:53,999
- Wow. Hey, your aim is good today.
- What, are you surprised?

746
00:47:56,368 --> 00:47:58,070
Hey, how are you so good?

747
00:47:59,137 --> 00:48:01,340
- I'll take care of it.
- One team left, one team.

748
00:48:02,874 --> 00:48:05,777
I smell chicken.

749
00:48:05,811 --> 00:48:07,245
What?

750
00:48:07,245 --> 00:48:09,448
I think we're going to win.

751
00:48:09,448 --> 00:48:11,049
(Winner! Winner! Chicken Dinner!)

752
00:48:11,617 --> 00:48:13,485
Chicken.

753
00:48:14,720 --> 00:48:16,088
How was it? It's fun when you win, right?

754
00:48:16,121 --> 00:48:18,156
This is so much fun.

755
00:48:19,725 --> 00:48:21,627
- This is really fun. Yes.
- Isn't it?

756
00:48:22,160 --> 00:48:26,064
Hey, thanks to you,
I feel like a huge weight has been lifted.

757
00:48:27,165 --> 00:48:28,200
You were great.

758
00:48:28,834 --> 00:48:30,636
- It wasn't me.
- What wasn't?

759
00:48:33,672 --> 00:48:35,841
What? Three kills?

760
00:48:36,642 --> 00:48:38,110
You only got three kills?

761
00:48:38,110 --> 00:48:39,244
Then how did we win?

762
00:48:40,012 --> 00:48:41,013
Let me see.

763
00:48:43,982 --> 00:48:46,451
Bo Na. What's that?

764
00:48:46,451 --> 00:48:47,653
Why?

765
00:48:47,653 --> 00:48:50,188
You killed all of them.

766
00:48:50,188 --> 00:48:51,456
You're not a beginner, are you?

767
00:48:51,456 --> 00:48:53,925
No, I think we just discovered
your hidden talent.

768
00:48:53,925 --> 00:48:56,528
Were you a sniper in a past life
or something?

769
00:48:57,596 --> 00:48:59,498
- Maybe I was.
- This is amazing.

770
00:48:59,498 --> 00:49:01,166
I was lucky today.

771
00:49:01,833 --> 00:49:03,669
How about one more round?

772
00:49:03,702 --> 00:49:05,537
- Really?
- Okay.

773
00:49:05,537 --> 00:49:06,872
Yes, I'd love to.

774
00:49:06,872 --> 00:49:08,807
This game isn't that easy.

775
00:49:28,727 --> 00:49:30,829
(bona_fide, Kills: 19)

776
00:49:31,897 --> 00:49:33,131
Goodness.

777
00:49:33,832 --> 00:49:35,567
This can't be right.

778
00:49:37,669 --> 00:49:41,139
Se Ah must have been so excited,
holding you back.

779
00:49:42,174 --> 00:49:44,176
I had so much fun.

780
00:49:44,843 --> 00:49:46,812
And I got to try a lot of new things.

781
00:49:46,812 --> 00:49:49,247
- It was a lot of fun.
- Sounds like Se Ah did a great job.

782
00:49:50,515 --> 00:49:53,151
It's okay, so take your time.

783
00:49:53,552 --> 00:49:55,554
I'm going to take Yul
to the restaurant later.

784
00:49:55,988 --> 00:49:57,322
My sister said to get fresh kimchi.

785
00:49:57,322 --> 00:49:59,458
Really? I love your mom's fresh kimchi.

786
00:49:59,458 --> 00:50:01,893
- Bring a lot, okay?
- Today, I...

787
00:50:01,927 --> 00:50:03,528
saw a new side of her...

788
00:50:03,528 --> 00:50:05,230
which was so shocking
that it blew my mind.

789
00:50:05,797 --> 00:50:06,865
Wasn't she so cool?

790
00:50:07,299 --> 00:50:09,301
How old did you say your niece was?

791
00:50:09,968 --> 00:50:11,703
Yul? Four. Why?

792
00:50:12,804 --> 00:50:15,107
Then the timing is perfect.

793
00:50:16,642 --> 00:50:17,876
You know I have good instincts, right?

794
00:50:17,909 --> 00:50:19,611
You do?

795
00:50:20,379 --> 00:50:21,713
I really think your sister-in-law...

796
00:50:24,850 --> 00:50:26,652
is hiding her true identity.

797
00:50:27,119 --> 00:50:28,153
Her true identity?

798
00:50:29,087 --> 00:50:31,857
The one who suddenly vanished
in the spring four years ago...

799
00:50:34,993 --> 00:50:37,663
- The legend of the FPS game.
- She was on maternity leave.

800
00:50:39,031 --> 00:50:40,365
Someone who appears
once every few years...

801
00:50:40,365 --> 00:50:42,501
and sweeps the top records.
A gaming prodigy?

802
00:50:42,968 --> 00:50:44,169
That's ridiculous.

803
00:50:46,571 --> 00:50:47,572
I guess not.

804
00:50:49,207 --> 00:50:50,208
Mm.

805
00:50:50,642 --> 00:50:52,210
- Hey, about today...
- Yes?

806
00:50:52,244 --> 00:50:54,413
You were probably surprised when
I suddenly asked you to hang out, right?

807
00:50:55,180 --> 00:50:56,481
No, I was just...

808
00:50:57,649 --> 00:50:58,650
excited.

809
00:50:59,051 --> 00:51:02,621
It's been so long since I went out
by myself without Yul, so I was thrilled.

810
00:51:02,654 --> 00:51:04,423
- Really?
- Yes.

811
00:51:04,423 --> 00:51:07,459
So have you not seen any of your friends
since you had Yul?

812
00:51:08,627 --> 00:51:12,731
I guess I don't really have many friends.
I'm not sure why.

813
00:51:12,764 --> 00:51:15,567
- Oh, I see.
- Yes.

814
00:51:15,567 --> 00:51:20,005
You know, I feel like today,
you and I have gotten a step closer.

815
00:51:20,005 --> 00:51:21,907
- You think so?
- Yes.

816
00:51:21,940 --> 00:51:25,611
Actually, there was something
I wanted to ask you.

817
00:51:26,411 --> 00:51:28,480
That's part of the reason
I asked you to hang out.

818
00:51:29,681 --> 00:51:32,117
But I've changed my mind.

819
00:51:32,117 --> 00:51:34,186
I'm going to ask for
something else instead.

820
00:51:34,186 --> 00:51:35,387
What is it?

821
00:51:35,387 --> 00:51:38,924
From now on, you don't have
to be so formal with me.

822
00:51:38,924 --> 00:51:40,092
Ah.

823
00:51:40,125 --> 00:51:44,329
I'm your younger sister-in-law,
and we're family.

824
00:51:46,732 --> 00:51:48,400
Okay, I can do that.

825
00:51:48,400 --> 00:51:51,403
Really? Awesome! Today was a success!

826
00:51:51,403 --> 00:51:53,405
Then can I link arms with you?

827
00:51:54,439 --> 00:51:56,808
- Sure. Go ahead.
- Really?

828
00:52:00,612 --> 00:52:01,913
This is nice.

829
00:52:01,947 --> 00:52:03,882
(Taesung Chicken)

830
00:52:03,882 --> 00:52:06,685
Mom, are you still mad?

831
00:52:07,219 --> 00:52:08,754
You really hold a grudge.

832
00:52:08,754 --> 00:52:12,124
It's not like that woman hasn't said
awful things before.

833
00:52:12,157 --> 00:52:15,060
But I guess you don't like it
when others insult your daughter-in-law?

834
00:52:15,060 --> 00:52:17,296
Of course I don't.

835
00:52:17,329 --> 00:52:19,031
She's my child now too.

836
00:52:19,031 --> 00:52:20,332
If anyone's going to criticize her,
it should be me.

837
00:52:20,332 --> 00:52:21,366
Who is she to judge?

838
00:52:22,200 --> 00:52:24,202
What? "Radiant?"

839
00:52:25,170 --> 00:52:26,872
Is she saying my girl is
all drab and dull?

840
00:52:26,905 --> 00:52:28,307
"Your girl?"

841
00:52:28,941 --> 00:52:32,344
That wretched woman.
Who said I wanted to brag about it?

842
00:52:32,344 --> 00:52:34,446
I didn't like having an orphan
for a daughter-in-law either,

843
00:52:34,446 --> 00:52:36,548
and I was annoyed we couldn't have
a formal meeting of the families.

844
00:52:36,949 --> 00:52:38,116
Mom.

845
00:52:38,150 --> 00:52:43,121
What mother in the world wants to give
her precious son to an orphan?

846
00:52:43,155 --> 00:52:45,657
- But as time went by...
- Mom.

847
00:52:58,503 --> 00:53:00,138
Oh, you're here.

848
00:53:00,606 --> 00:53:01,807
Yes, Mother.

849
00:53:03,842 --> 00:53:05,911
Oh, what are you all doing here together?

850
00:53:09,514 --> 00:53:11,083
Honey, take Yul and wait outside.

851
00:53:11,650 --> 00:53:13,852
- Why?
- Please, just wait outside.

852
00:53:16,288 --> 00:53:17,889
Mother, have this when you get hungry.

853
00:53:17,889 --> 00:53:18,991
I brought some
sweet red bean bread you like.

854
00:53:18,991 --> 00:53:20,926
All right. Thank you.

855
00:53:27,299 --> 00:53:28,300
(Chacha Sweet Red Bean Bread)

856
00:53:35,941 --> 00:53:38,677
You should've told me
you were coming together.

857
00:53:40,946 --> 00:53:42,381
Have you eaten dinner?

858
00:53:45,150 --> 00:53:46,385
Mom.

859
00:53:47,619 --> 00:53:48,920
Apologize to Yul's mom.

860
00:53:49,554 --> 00:53:50,622
What? I...

861
00:53:51,423 --> 00:53:54,359
It's not like I said it for her to hear.

862
00:53:54,359 --> 00:53:55,694
But she heard you.

863
00:53:58,096 --> 00:54:00,666
To be blunt, was I lying?

864
00:54:01,233 --> 00:54:03,402
It's true that she's an orphan.

865
00:54:03,435 --> 00:54:04,636
Mom.

866
00:54:05,504 --> 00:54:07,606
Being an orphan doesn't mean
you can treat her however you want.

867
00:54:08,607 --> 00:54:10,275
How am I treating her...

868
00:54:14,212 --> 00:54:17,249
So what are you going to do
if I refuse to apologize?

869
00:54:17,916 --> 00:54:19,751
What, are you going to
stop seeing me or something?

870
00:54:34,199 --> 00:54:38,470
My goodness. You raise a child,
and it's all for nothing.

871
00:54:38,503 --> 00:54:40,639
All he cares about is his precious wife.

872
00:54:41,940 --> 00:54:42,941
Mom.

873
00:54:44,443 --> 00:54:45,644
Honestly, you feel bad, don't you?

874
00:54:45,677 --> 00:54:47,179
Sorry? What would I be sorry about?

875
00:54:48,013 --> 00:54:50,515
You can bad-mouth anyone behind.
What did I do?

876
00:54:52,751 --> 00:54:55,587
Why did they have to burst in
at that exact moment?

877
00:54:58,223 --> 00:55:00,392
Such crappy timing.

878
00:55:07,566 --> 00:55:08,900
I'm sorry.

879
00:55:08,900 --> 00:55:10,302
I'll apologize on my mom's behalf.

880
00:55:12,738 --> 00:55:14,906
Me? I'm okay.

881
00:55:15,841 --> 00:55:17,009
It doesn't bother me at all.

882
00:55:20,879 --> 00:55:24,650
Your mother is a mother, after all.
Maybe it's because I'm a mother now too?

883
00:55:24,650 --> 00:55:27,386
I think... I kind of understand.

884
00:55:29,288 --> 00:55:31,256
How your heart wavers
when it comes to your child.

885
00:55:32,758 --> 00:55:35,394
How you always put your own child first.

886
00:55:41,366 --> 00:55:45,137
Being a mother doesn't excuse everything.
She was in the wrong.

887
00:55:49,174 --> 00:55:51,143
Well then, should I make a real scene?

888
00:55:52,411 --> 00:55:54,146
Isn't your mom going too far?

889
00:55:56,181 --> 00:55:59,151
I mean, I'm not the same person
I was back then.

890
00:55:59,618 --> 00:56:03,055
I'm not alone anymore.
I have a husband and a daughter,

891
00:56:03,055 --> 00:56:05,824
and a mother-in-law
and three sisters-in-law.

892
00:56:06,491 --> 00:56:08,860
What's important is the present,
not the past, right?

893
00:56:13,899 --> 00:56:14,900
But...

894
00:56:16,802 --> 00:56:18,770
I believe she'll understand someday.

895
00:56:19,471 --> 00:56:21,607
You know, if we just keep
hashing things out like this...

896
00:56:23,942 --> 00:56:25,143
You know expressions like that?

897
00:56:26,912 --> 00:56:29,548
Well, you know,
crying and laughing together,

898
00:56:30,515 --> 00:56:31,717
getting on each other's nerves,

899
00:56:32,618 --> 00:56:33,986
and hurting each other.

900
00:56:35,187 --> 00:56:36,588
Isn't that what it's all about?

901
00:56:38,023 --> 00:56:40,459
So we're hashing things out right now.
That's right.

902
00:56:42,628 --> 00:56:44,329
Stir-fry? What are you stir-frying?

903
00:56:45,797 --> 00:56:47,332
What does our Yul want to stir-fry?

904
00:56:47,766 --> 00:56:49,401
How about we stir-fry
some sausage you like?

905
00:56:49,434 --> 00:56:51,036
Yes, I love sausage.

906
00:56:51,837 --> 00:56:55,240
- Let's go make some sausage.
- Let's go make some sausage.

907
00:57:22,629 --> 00:57:23,630
The lights are off?

908
00:57:24,965 --> 00:57:25,966
Did they close already?

909
00:57:30,270 --> 00:57:32,873
They didn't even lock the door?
What's going on?

910
00:57:58,665 --> 00:58:01,134
Mom.

911
00:58:02,869 --> 00:58:03,870
Dad.

912
00:58:28,862 --> 00:58:30,063
Is it 50 percent off for the set?

913
00:58:30,497 --> 00:58:31,631
Yes, welcome.

914
00:58:31,631 --> 00:58:34,668
- Yes, can I help you with anything?
- I'm just looking.

915
00:58:34,668 --> 00:58:35,869
Yes, go ahead.

916
00:58:37,537 --> 00:58:40,173
It's 50 percent.
But please write down your address.

917
00:58:40,173 --> 00:58:43,543
- Yes, we'll send out the first shipment.
- Okay.

918
00:58:43,543 --> 00:58:45,779
(Dongwoon Furniture,
We have the lowest prices.)

919
00:58:45,812 --> 00:58:47,514
You'll have to pay here.

920
00:58:47,547 --> 00:58:48,548
I'm back.

921
00:58:53,987 --> 00:58:56,323
You left for that delivery a while ago.
What took you so long?

922
00:58:57,557 --> 00:58:59,626
You weren't messing around somewhere,
were you?

923
00:58:59,659 --> 00:59:03,029
No, sir. I took a wrong turn on the way...

924
00:59:03,697 --> 00:59:06,366
- I'm sorry.
- And what did you do to the chair...

925
00:59:06,366 --> 00:59:08,535
you delivered to Taeheung-dong
this morning?

926
00:59:08,535 --> 00:59:11,538
We got a complaint that
one of its legs is wobbly.

927
00:59:11,538 --> 00:59:15,242
What? That can't be right.

928
00:59:15,275 --> 00:59:17,244
I told you to be careful
when you're loading and unloading things.

929
00:59:17,244 --> 00:59:21,615
How many times do I have to tell you?
Why do you always make us do repairs?

930
00:59:22,082 --> 00:59:24,885
How am I supposed to keep giving you work
if you keep this up?

931
00:59:25,786 --> 00:59:27,988
I'm sorry. It won't happen again.

932
00:59:28,021 --> 00:59:30,056
Whatever.
Just get back to work.

933
00:59:30,557 --> 00:59:31,558
Goodness.

934
00:59:32,058 --> 00:59:33,093
I'm sorry.

935
00:59:34,661 --> 00:59:37,397
That prick is always on my case.

936
00:59:38,698 --> 00:59:40,367
(Dongwoon Furniture,
We have the lowest prices.)

937
00:59:45,172 --> 00:59:46,673
(Dongwoon Furniture)

938
00:59:56,016 --> 00:59:58,051
(Dongwoon Furniture)

939
01:00:10,230 --> 01:00:13,133
(Dongwoon Furniture)

940
01:01:14,661 --> 01:01:16,763
That bastard.

941
01:01:17,197 --> 01:01:19,466
(Dongwoon Furniture,
We have the lowest prices.)

942
01:01:19,499 --> 01:01:20,500
(Dongwoon Furniture)

943
01:01:36,383 --> 01:01:37,417
Hey.

944
01:01:39,853 --> 01:01:41,688
Die, you bastard.

945
01:01:43,557 --> 01:01:45,092
Honey!

946
01:01:46,827 --> 01:01:50,063
Why do you look down on people?

947
01:01:50,097 --> 01:01:52,632
Why? Why?

948
01:01:53,333 --> 01:01:54,334
You bastard.

949
01:01:57,604 --> 01:02:00,140
Police. Drop the knife, Jang Eun Hak.

950
01:02:06,413 --> 01:02:10,484
Go on, shoot. Shoot me, you bastard!

951
01:02:10,484 --> 01:02:12,786
If you want to see this bitch die.

952
01:02:12,786 --> 01:02:14,821
Please help me.

953
01:02:14,855 --> 01:02:17,057
Please help me. Please.

954
01:02:21,461 --> 01:02:22,629
This is your last warning.

955
01:02:23,663 --> 01:02:25,065
Drop the knife, Jang Eun Hak.

956
01:02:25,065 --> 01:02:27,067
Who the hell are you
to tell me what to do?

957
01:02:27,067 --> 01:02:28,635
You fucking bastard.

958
01:02:28,635 --> 01:02:32,005
- It's my knife! I'll do what I want!
- Jang Eun Hak.

959
01:02:32,005 --> 01:02:34,541
Please help me. Please.

960
01:02:35,242 --> 01:02:36,243
Please help me.

961
01:02:37,210 --> 01:02:38,678
Please help me.

962
01:02:40,147 --> 01:02:41,314
Let her go.

963
01:02:41,948 --> 01:02:45,819
All the bastards in the world
who look down on me,

964
01:02:45,819 --> 01:02:49,122
I'm going to kill them all.
Every last one of them. You hear me?

965
01:02:49,122 --> 01:02:50,357
Hey, you looked down on me too,
didn't you?

966
01:02:50,791 --> 01:02:53,059
You...

967
01:02:59,299 --> 01:03:00,467
Drop the knife, Jang Eun Hak.

968
01:03:00,467 --> 01:03:01,768
Honey.

969
01:03:01,768 --> 01:03:03,103
Oh, what do I do?

970
01:03:09,242 --> 01:03:10,243
Jang Eun Hak.

971
01:03:13,580 --> 01:03:16,750
Apply pressure to the wound
and call 911 now. Hurry!

972
01:03:19,019 --> 01:03:20,020
(Dongwoon Furniture,
We have the lowest prices.)

973
01:03:29,096 --> 01:03:30,097
Hey!

974
01:03:45,212 --> 01:03:46,346
Hey, you bastard, stop right there!

975
01:03:52,152 --> 01:03:53,186
Jang Eun Hak!

976
01:03:59,760 --> 01:04:00,761
Hey!

977
01:04:04,197 --> 01:04:05,198
Stop!

978
01:04:07,534 --> 01:04:09,169
Jang Eun Hak, stop!

979
01:04:10,670 --> 01:04:11,772
Jang Eun Hak, stop!

980
01:04:14,040 --> 01:04:15,542
Mom!

981
01:04:26,019 --> 01:04:27,020
Dong Jin!

982
01:05:23,877 --> 01:05:28,014
(A Bona Fide Killer)

983
01:05:28,515 --> 01:05:29,716
Dong Jin!

984
01:05:30,484 --> 01:05:33,687
<i>What if you run into your husband?</i>

985
01:05:33,687 --> 01:05:36,256
<i>Tae Sung, what should I do? I...</i>

986
01:05:36,256 --> 01:05:38,325
<i>You should get out of there now.</i>

987
01:05:38,325 --> 01:05:41,795
<i>Your escape route was too broad,</i>
<i>so I'm not sure if it covered everything.</i>

988
01:05:41,795 --> 01:05:44,464
So you're saying we won't know
what to expect.

989
01:05:44,464 --> 01:05:45,999
<i>Guess what I found.</i>

990
01:05:45,999 --> 01:05:48,235
Mom!

991
01:05:48,235 --> 01:05:51,772
<i>Dong Jin,</i>
<i>the law isn't perfect. You know that.</i>

992
01:05:51,805 --> 01:05:53,473
<i>I'm going to do my job,</i>

993
01:05:53,507 --> 01:05:55,442
<i>so you do yours. You're a reporter.</i>

994
01:05:56,143 --> 01:05:57,577
<i>My husband does his job,</i>

995
01:05:58,078 --> 01:05:59,579
<i>and I do mine.</i>

996
01:06:04,184 --> 01:06:06,186
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
